# Your own secrets. `.env.example` is the committed template; `.env` is the copy
# of it that holds a real ADMINIUM_SECRET, and README.md tells every reader to
# make one — so it is ignored here rather than left to whoever types `git add .`.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Scratch output of the provenance build in src/builtOutput.test.ts — the same
# app built a second time with sourcemaps, so the ban grep can tell a
# dependency chunk from one of ours. Evidence, not output; deleted after use.
.provenance
